    feat(battery): bwrap-vs-unshare backend parity battery + measured limits (TJ-GAP-056)
    
    specs/cli.md section 4 ended at "a bwrap-specific containment battery is
    TJ-GAP-056" with no shipped battery and no measured parity evidence: the
    bwrap backend (TJ-GAP-054) was covered by PATH-stub unit tests for argv and
    selection semantics only, and nothing pinned the one property where the two
    backends genuinely differ (the private /proc). A backend swap must be
    proven, not assumed.
    
    Ships the battery, the measured evidence, and the regression contracts:
    
    - scripts/backend-parity-battery.py — a host-classifying battery in the
      probe house style (always exits 0, never gates; --json for structured
      cells). Ten cells across the seven required measurements: private /proc
      per backend, orphan teardown per backend (SIGKILL the wrapper, payload
      found by exact cmdline diff, latency measured), escape-wave replay under
      the bwrap backend (engine corpus via pytest, tail line recorded, plus a
      live-wrapper argv/exit slice), the DEGRADED fail-closed contract for both
      backends (PATH-stubbed probe failure -> exit 2, command not run, marker
      file the payload would have created stays ABSENT — host-independent by
      construction), and the pidns/fs-isolation host classification. Verdict
      vocabulary: SAME | DIFFERS | KNOWN-LIMIT | FAIL-CLOSED-PROVEN; a cell
      that cannot be measured is labelled KNOWN-LIMIT/UNMEASURED, never guessed.
    
    - docs/backend-parity.md — the measured numbers for this host (kernel
      7.0.0-30-generic, bubblewrap 0.11.1, jail /proc 4 vs host ~1340, unshare
      --user /proc 1344, both orphan teardowns 20 ms, escape replay "221 passed
      in 0.95s"), the verbatim parity table, cell-by-cell provenance notes,
      known limits (a)-(d), and a re-run block. Zero unexplained divergences.
    
    - plugin/test_backend_parity.py — durable contracts: fail-closed for both
      backends (PATH stub + TJ_BWRAP_PROBE_EXIT + marker-absence, plus
      probe-only launch proof), the three parity-relevant argv invariants not
      already owned by test_backend_selection.py (--proc /proc present,
      --die-with-parent present, --as-pid-1 absent), the battery subprocess
      exit-0/table/vocabulary pins, and host-conditional live cells that skip
      with grep-able HOST-DEGRADED-BWRAP / HOST-DEGRADED-PIDNS markers.
    
    - specs/cli.md — the TJ-GAP-056 placeholder now points at the shipped
      battery and doc; the section, its table, and the backend contract are
      otherwise untouched.
    
    Measured findings worth knowing (details in docs/backend-parity.md):
    the unshare --user jail exposes the host /proc while bwrap's --proc /proc
    does not (the one genuine divergence, documented, not a failure); orphan
    teardown is equivalent on this host (both dead within 20 ms of the
    wrapper's SIGKILL); both backends fail closed identically; and raw
    bwrap --bind / / --unshare-pid WITHOUT --proc /proc still shows the host
    procfs (1348 entries measured) — hand-rolled probes that omit the flag
    measure the wrong thing. TERMINAL_JAIL_INTERRUPTOR_MODE=disabled flips
    105 of the 221 escape-wave verdicts to allow, so the replay cell runs
    under the default mode.
    
